# Everything below is excluded from every image build context. All four
# Dockerfiles (apps/{api,web,portal,worker}/Dockerfile) do a `COPY . .` in
# their `build` stage, so without this file a build run from a developer
# machine copies the host's own artifacts straight into the image:
#
#   - `node_modules/` (and every per-package `node_modules/`) would overwrite
#     the Linux dependency tree the `deps` stage just installed with the
#     host's — on Windows/macOS that means native binaries (esbuild, @swc,
#     Prisma engines, sharp) built for the wrong platform.
#   - `.env` / `.env.local` are gitignored *secrets*; `COPY . .` would bake
#     them into a published image layer. Worse, Next.js loads `.env.local`
#     during `next build`, so a stale local `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` could end
#     up compiled into a production browser bundle.
#   - `.next/`, `dist/`, `.turbo/`, `*.tsbuildinfo` are stale build output
#     that either gets rebuilt anyway or silently shadows the real build.
#
# CI builds from a fresh `actions/checkout` and therefore never had any of
# these, which is exactly why the problem was invisible there.

# --- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# --- Secrets / local environment -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.turbo
.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/api/generated

# --- VCS / tooling ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.squad
.vscode
.idea

# --- Tests / reports -------------------------------------------------------
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# --- Docs & local-only compose --------------------------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
.dockerignore
